    {
      "id": "claim_8e8d438f1a6c48d3a84aae4352876307",
      "statement": "ConsentsGate (src/ConsentsGate.tsx) renders above the router in App.tsx, wrapping the entire route tree. This placement is essential because a blocked user has no valid session — /users/me is also refused by the 451 rule — so AuthGuard would bounce them to login before they could see the acceptance form.",
      "evidence": [
