        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b5e8bdf1ada54adc81793c6eb7accc54",
      "statement": "When the user checks both ToS and Privacy Policy boxes and clicks 'I accept', ConsentsGate calls auth.acceptConsents() which sends a PATCH to /users/{userId} with an empty consents array — the client states nothing about versions. The server's permission stamps the current versions and timestamp via mergeRequest. Then auth.checkSession() reloads the user document (now unblocked) and the blocked flag is cleared.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rhc.setup.consents.ts#L194-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56499f2d0ad5eed28fb40c71ad06fe70a7a4e81e66811d8d67d473627ab1b050:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/ConsentsGate.tsx#L33-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36821e11be376177dcd4b12efe71f864ef22254c37efae989582b05cea96fbf5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08295ed978dc4816b6ab0df6f9284195",
      "statement": "The consents gate server-side setup (rhc.setup.consents.ts) extends the base accounts setup with four steps: a user schema validation, an acceptance permission that stamps latestConsents and pushes to consents history, token claims configuration (latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp in account-properties-claims), and a Guards rule with status 451 that blocks authenticated users whose consents don't match the current version strings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rhc.setup.consents.ts#L167-L294",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dbe7b85b707589d175941a57a6fe044d469d3c76b3ea6bf52694bd9d21330015:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_967850bb3d2f407db71741b04933b475",
      "statement": "Version strings TOS_VERSION and PP_VERSION are defined once in rhc.setup.consents.ts and derived everywhere else — in the permission's mergeRequest and in the guard rule's condition. Bumping them and re-running rhc setup requires all users to accept again. The acceptance history is preserved in the consents array on each user document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://rhc.setup.consents.ts#L134-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:152607e653da37f5f18e11d56b3e53c87e63a611c2dfc3bc59005995c4e38be8:"
